# What never belongs in a build context. None of it is copied by any of the
# four image files, and `.venv` and `data/` are gigabytes each: without this
# every `docker build` here ships the local virtual environment and, on a
# machine that has run the pipeline, the lake, to the daemon before the first
# instruction runs.
#
# `data/` is the one that matters beyond speed. It is gitignored and may hold
# the real lake, so an image built on a laptop must not be able to carry it
# even by accident.
.venv/
data/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
